🐛 Describe the bug
Hi,
I found a bug during testing with libFuzzer.
It is located at  /pytorch_fuzz/torch/csrc/jit/serialization/unpickler.cpp in several places of readInstruction() function.
Apparently, the error is related to incorrectly use of marks_ and stack_ fields when reading malformed model via torch::jit::load() function. There are several crash-files that trigger this bug, which may be resulted in throwing unhandled std::out_of_range exception, heap buffer overflow Asan message or segmentation fault.
The bug could be reproduced with aot_model_compiler binary:
aot_model_compiler --model=crash-file --model_name=name --model_version=1 --input_dims='1,3,224,224;2,2' --input_types='float;float'

